## In overall Do not wheel-- we only consider EPS or P/E ration... can we consider below where fundamentally companies are not skipped.. Also skip non-profitable or negative companies.. Add these into Do not wheel and keep checking every week/month only
The Fundamental Rule: Metric Matching
Instead of replacing P/E with PEG, match the metric to the company lifecycle stage:

Company Type	Growth Profile	Primary Valuation Metrics	Why
High Growth	EPS Growth >15%	PEG + EV/Sales	Captures growth trajectory relative to valuation.
Mature / Value	EPS Growth 0%−8%	Forward P/E + Free Cash Flow Yield	Growth is low; focus is on earnings consistency and cash return.
Capital Intensive	High Depreciation / Debt	EV/EBITDA	Strips out non-cash charges and capital structure differences.
Early Stage / Unprofitable	Negative EPS	EV/Revenue + Gross Margin	P/E and PEG are mathematically unusable.
Filter Parameter	Threshold / Metric	Why It Filters Out Loss-Makers
Trailing EPS (Net Income)	>0 (or Positive)	Eliminates companies reporting a net loss over the past 12 months.
Forward EPS Estimate	>0 (or Positive)	Ensures analysts project the company to stay profitable over the next 12 months.
Operating Income (EBIT)	>0 (or Positive)	Verifies the core business makes money before taxes, interest, or one-off accounting items.
Free Cash Flow (FCF)	>0 (Positive FCF)	The ultimate truth test: Ensures the business generates actual cash flow after paying for operations and capital expenditures.